{%- comment -%}
  Atomically move ONE pending approval to a decided status (spec §9.6). Every
  decision path (operator approve / reject / bulk-reject, agent cancel) goes through
  here so two concurrent decisions can never both act on the same row — e.g. a
  double-clicked Approve executing the handler twice, or a reject landing while an
  approval is already executing.

  platformOS Liquid has no compare-and-set and {% transaction %} is READ COMMITTED,
  so we serialize with the row itself: the FIRST op in the transaction rewrites
  claim_token with a fresh unique value (a real UPDATE → row-write-lock held until
  commit). A concurrent claim blocks there, then re-reads the row we committed and
  sees it is no longer pending.

  @param {string} id             - approval record id
  @param {string} handle         - approval handle (for the locked re-read)
  @param {string} status         - target status (approved | rejected | cancelled | expired)
  @param {string} decided_by
  @param {string} result_summary
  @return {object} { claimed:boolean, rec } rec = the row as re-read under the lock
{%- endcomment -%}
{% liquid
  function object = 'modules/mcp/commands/approval/claim/build', id: id, handle: handle, status: status, decided_by: decided_by, result_summary: result_summary
  function object = 'modules/mcp/commands/approval/claim/check', object: object
  if object.valid
    function out = 'modules/mcp/commands/approval/claim/execute', object: object
    return out
  endif

  assign out = {
    "claimed": false,
    "rec": null
  }
  return out
%}
